WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.319 --> 00:00:18.090
STUDENT: I had two slightly related questions-- 

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:25.090
I guess the first one is, we were talking about how--  

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:29.130
well, this could be the resurgence of religion is-- 

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:36.130
could be the last gasp of religion. And I was wondering what exactly are the

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:43.780
proofs or justifications of that? Especially when we were talking about how, because of globalization, 

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:50.000
people are looking back to religion and relying more and more on it. And I guess I'll pose my other question later. 

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.070
VOLF: Yeah.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:02.880
So what are some of the indicators? 

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:08.550
Well, I mean, you can-- say, take Europe as paradigmatic. 

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.870
What's gonna happen

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.680
as

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:18.670
countries develop, as nations develop, in the course of globalization processes?

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:24.560
Well, you can look at Sweden. I think the church attendance is about 2-3%. 

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.400
You look

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:32.900
at Great Britain, I think church attendance there is somewhere around 5 or so percent? 

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:38.450
And you can go down the line. Not just true of the Protestant 

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:43.120
nations, it's also true of the Catholic ones. In Italy, it's dropping rapidly; in 

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.850
Spain, it's dropping rapidly. 

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:47.750
These countries are secularizing, 

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:53.050
and the theory then was: this is really what happens when you give modernization

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:56.220
a chance, right? Just let it sit for a while

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.159
and have its impact, 

00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:03.509
it's going to erode religious convictions. 

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:04.700
That's often paired

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.799
with the idea of what function

00:02:06.799 --> 00:02:07.579
it is

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:10.469
that religion fulfills, right?

00:02:10.469 --> 00:02:13.130
And the claim that these functions

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:17.489
 that religion in primitive societies for primitive people fulfilled-- 

00:02:17.489 --> 00:02:22.319
will be fulfilled, we can show how they will be fulfilled, by other-- 

00:02:22.319 --> 00:02:27.939
by forces of modernization. Easy access to medicine, 

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:34.689
social care, and so forth and so forth. And you will basically not need

00:02:34.689 --> 00:02:36.409
religion. So you have an account of 

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:37.950
how societies develop,

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.679
and what it is that creates a need for religion, 

00:02:40.679 --> 00:02:41.910
and you say, "Well, 

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.590
it's most likely that's exactly what's gonna happen

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:46.209
in other countries as well."

00:02:46.209 --> 00:02:50.129
So that's, I think, roughly-- and sociologists of religion, 

00:02:50.129 --> 00:02:54.650
great sociologists, have believed this for roughly 200 years, you know? 

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:56.549
So 

00:02:56.549 --> 00:03:02.309
we are now realizing that that might not be the case, and only recently we have these theories

00:03:02.309 --> 00:03:04.489
of multiple modernities, 

00:03:04.489 --> 00:03:07.089
studying very carefully how different societies

00:03:07.089 --> 00:03:11.419
modernize and what happens to them when they modernize. 

00:03:11.419 --> 00:03:14.599
United States was seen as always as an anomaly, 

00:03:14.599 --> 00:03:19.029
and needed some explaining, and explanations were offered-- but Europe was the paradigm. Now

00:03:19.029 --> 00:03:21.760
Now it's inverted. Now the United States seems more like a--

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:22.780
 as a paradigm, 

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:23.659
and Europe,

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:27.319
for whatever reason, is seen to be anomalous in terms of developments 

00:03:27.319 --> 00:03:28.230
because we see 

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:32.629
analogous things happening in other countries as we see in the United States. 

00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:35.629
Now, that's on this side, right?

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:37.769
Contest on the side 

00:03:37.769 --> 00:03:39.989
of advocate of multiple modernities. 

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:43.450
Others will say, "Even the United States-- give it time.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.559
It's gonna go down. 

00:03:45.559 --> 00:03:49.079
And some indicators are there that

00:03:49.079 --> 00:03:53.649
religious observance, for whatever reasons, is over-reported in the United States.

00:03:53.649 --> 00:03:56.949
The United States is much less religious of a country

00:03:56.949 --> 00:04:00.519
 than it's claimed that it is. So the debate goes back and forth. 

